  "factor": "At first order decision use the last completed five-minute bar close. Compute one-hour log returns on the exact grid, and take the median across the 39 non-BTC contracts requiring at least 32 valid. Compare it to the RMS of the previous 168 non-overlapping one-hour median returns at the same minute phase. Market shock requires signed median z <= -1.5 and at least two-thirds of available alts moving against the side. BTC comparator uses its own RMS and the same signed z threshold without a breadth clause. If either z is missing, retain as unknown and exclude from all comparative event groups.",
  "markout": "Signed worst adverse move measured from the mark OPEN at actual first fill over the next 72 five-minute mark OPEN ticks, regardless of actual exit. A >=3% adverse move is the tail outcome. Use same 40-pair universe. Do not combine cost accounts as independent evidence. Keep censoring and native final trade PnL separate from markout.",
  "gate": "For both costs in both windows require at least 12 market-shock and 12 BTC shock distinct UTC dates in 2024 and at least 18 each in later window. Day-balanced median marked MAE must be >=0.75pp higher when market flags vs not. Day-balanced mean tail hit rate must exceed BTC by at least 5pp. For 2024 shadow sizing, halve market-flagged full native positions at fixed fills, fills times, sizes of all other positions, exits, and account paths. Require <=25% observed 5m drawdown, lower than original 2x, and >=60% of 2x incremental full return over original 1x retained at both costs. Only joint pass justifies a separate native account experiment. Shadow scaling is an additive attribution, with no new wallet or compounding dynamics.",
  "known_history": "The original profits and April 2024 risk episode were known. Conditional markouts and shadow results were unknown. Later ledgers are fixed native 1x cohorts and window transfer is retrospective, not an independent 2x account.",
  "orders_enabled": false
